WEBVTT

00:00.660 --> 00:01.900
Matthew 9

00:01.900 --> 00:07.320
And getting into a boat, he crossed over, and came to his own city.

00:08.160 --> 00:11.820
And behold, some people brought to him a paralytic lying on a bed.

00:12.140 --> 00:15.600
And when Jesus saw their faith, he said to the paralytic,

00:16.180 --> 00:19.660
Take heart, my son, your sins are forgiven.

00:20.540 --> 00:23.580
And behold, some of the scribes said to themselves,

00:24.380 --> 00:26.280
This man is blaspheming.

00:26.280 --> 00:30.420
But Jesus, knowing their thoughts, said,

00:31.500 --> 00:33.880
Why do you think evil in your hearts?

00:34.360 --> 00:39.640
For which is easier to say, Your sins are forgiven, or to say, Rise and walk?

00:40.160 --> 00:44.460
But that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins.

00:45.220 --> 00:47.060
He then said to the paralytic,

00:47.920 --> 00:50.880
Rise, pick up your bed, and go home.

00:51.420 --> 00:53.960
And he rose and went home.

00:54.300 --> 00:56.260
When the crowd saw it, they were afraid.

00:56.660 --> 01:01.200
And they glorified God, who had given such authority to men.

01:02.080 --> 01:06.680
As Jesus passed on from there, he saw a man called Matthew sitting at the tax booth.

01:06.960 --> 01:07.920
And he said to him,

01:08.580 --> 01:09.580
Follow me.

01:10.220 --> 01:12.220
And he rose and followed him.

01:12.980 --> 01:15.860
And as Jesus reclined at table in the house,

01:16.340 --> 01:21.620
behold, many tax collectors and sinners came and were reclining with Jesus and his disciples.

01:22.200 --> 01:24.260
And when the Pharisees saw this,

01:24.260 --> 01:26.260
they said to his disciples,

01:26.820 --> 01:30.940
Why does your teacher eat with tax collectors and sinners?

01:31.840 --> 01:33.620
But when he heard it, he said,

01:34.660 --> 01:38.660
Those who are well have no need of a physician, but those who are sick.

01:39.360 --> 01:41.060
Go and learn what this means.

01:41.520 --> 01:44.140
I desire mercy and not sacrifice.

01:44.700 --> 01:47.960
For I came not to call the righteous, but sinners.

01:48.900 --> 01:51.360
Then the disciples of John came to him, saying,

01:51.780 --> 01:56.260
Why do we and the Pharisees fast, but your disciples do not fast?

01:56.820 --> 01:58.820
And Jesus said to them,

01:59.340 --> 02:02.940
Can the wedding guests mourn as long as the bridegroom is with them?

02:03.400 --> 02:08.440
The days will come when the bridegroom is taken away from them, and then they will fast.

02:09.340 --> 02:16.620
No one puts a piece of unshrunk cloth on an old garment, for the patch tears away from the garment, and a worse tear is made.

02:17.420 --> 02:25.680
Neither is new wine put into old wineskins. If it is, the skins burst, and the wine is spilled, and the skins are destroyed.

02:26.280 --> 02:31.100
But new wine is put into fresh wineskins, and so both are preserved.

02:32.980 --> 02:38.320
While he was saying these things to them, behold, a ruler came in and knelt before him, saying,

02:38.820 --> 02:46.500
My daughter has just died, but come and lay your hand on her, and she will live.

02:47.300 --> 02:49.620
And Jesus rose and followed him with his disciples.

02:50.180 --> 02:55.600
And behold, a woman who had suffered from a discharge of blood for twelve years came up behind him,

02:55.600 --> 02:57.920
and touched the fringe of his garment.

02:58.420 --> 02:59.900
For she said to herself,

03:00.780 --> 03:04.900
If I only touch his garment, I will be made well.

03:05.720 --> 03:08.640
Jesus turned, and seeing her, he said,

03:09.440 --> 03:12.940
Take heart, daughter, your faith has made you well.

03:13.740 --> 03:17.200
And instantly the woman was made well.

03:17.940 --> 03:23.140
And when Jesus came to the ruler's house and saw the flute players and the crowd making a commotion,

03:23.140 --> 03:24.080
he said,

03:24.240 --> 03:25.140
Go away.

03:25.600 --> 03:29.380
Go away, for the girl is not dead, but sleeping.

03:30.000 --> 03:31.980
And they laughed at him.

03:32.440 --> 03:37.280
But when the crowd had been put outside, he went in and took her by the hand,

03:37.600 --> 03:42.540
and the girl arose, and the report of this went through all that district.

03:43.740 --> 03:49.400
And as Jesus passed on from there, two blind men followed him, crying aloud,

03:50.320 --> 03:54.020
Have mercy on us, son of David.

03:54.520 --> 03:55.560
When he entered,

03:55.600 --> 03:56.140
the house,

03:56.460 --> 03:57.820
the blind men came to him.

03:58.340 --> 03:59.740
And Jesus said to them,

04:00.500 --> 04:03.080
Do you believe that I am able to do this?

04:03.780 --> 04:04.880
They said to him,

04:05.580 --> 04:06.660
Yes, Lord.

04:07.280 --> 04:10.360
Then he touched their eyes, saying,

04:11.140 --> 04:13.880
According to your faith, be it done to you.

04:14.540 --> 04:16.660
And their eyes were opened.

04:17.200 --> 04:18.980
And Jesus sternly warned them,

04:19.780 --> 04:21.960
See that no one knows about it.

04:22.140 --> 04:25.440
But they went away and spread his fame through,

04:25.600 --> 04:26.760
all that district.

04:27.760 --> 04:29.200
As they were going away,

04:29.840 --> 04:34.080
behold, a demon-oppressed man who was mute was brought to him.

04:34.660 --> 04:36.920
And when the demon had been cast out,

04:36.920 --> 04:38.900
the mute man spoke.

04:39.380 --> 04:41.080
And the crowds marveled, saying,

04:41.880 --> 04:44.500
Never was anything like this seen in Israel.

04:45.340 --> 04:47.360
But the Pharisees said,

04:48.120 --> 04:51.280
He casts out demons by the prince of demons.

04:52.700 --> 04:55.580
And Jesus went throughout all the cities and villages,

04:55.600 --> 04:59.160
teaching in their synagogues and proclaiming the gospel of the kingdom

04:59.160 --> 05:02.300
and healing every disease and every affliction.

05:02.980 --> 05:05.600
When he saw the crowds, he had compassion for them

05:05.600 --> 05:09.640
because they were harassed and helpless like sheep without a shepherd.

05:10.240 --> 05:11.760
Then he said to his disciples,

05:12.160 --> 05:16.620
The harvest is plentiful, but the laborers are few.

05:17.420 --> 05:20.180
Therefore pray earnestly to the Lord of the harvest

05:20.180 --> 05:22.960
to send out laborers into his harvest.

